course: dictionary
lesson: 1105
title: One word, three meanings: brand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A brand is the name a company gives its products, often with a logo, so you can tell who made them. «Every evening an orangutan climbs high, bends branches into a springy platform and piles leaves on top.» Here the word is not about a company at all, so the clues in the sentence will help. Read on to see which meaning fits.
explain: «The next night it builds a brand-new bed.» Brand-new means completely new, never used. The word brand joins with new to make a stronger word. Check your idea by swapping it into the sentence: the bed was never used before.
explain: Brand can also be a verb, a doing word. To brand something means to mark it with a brand, or to give someone a bad name. «He was branded a liar.» The clues are the word liar, which is bad, so branded here means given a bad name, not burned with a mark.
explain: Context clues work for brands in shops too. «A shop's own-brand product is often almost the same as the famous brand but cheaper, because you pay extra for the name and the adverts.» When you compare two products, ask which one you are paying for: the food, or the name and the adverts.
fact: A brand is the name, logo or mark that shows who made a product.
fact: «Brand new» means completely new, never used.
fact: To brand something means to mark it with a brand, or to give someone a bad name.
fact: On farms, cattle are branded: a mark is burned into the skin to show who owns them.
fact: A famous brand is not always better, because an own-brand product can be almost the same and cheaper.
exercise: Maya buys a brand of cereal from the shop. What is a brand? | A junk message sent to phones | A kind of cloud | A mark burned into an animal's skin | *The name of a product made by a company
exercise: «Every night it builds a brand-new bed.» What does brand-new mean? | Painted bright red | *Completely new, never used | Made of wood | Old and worn out
exercise: «He was branded a liar.» What does branded mean here? | Painted with a logo | *Given a bad name | Burned with a mark | Named after a company
test: What does it mean to brand cattle on a farm? | *Burn a mark into the skin to show who owns the animal | Sell them at the market | Feed them every morning | Move them to a new field
test: «A shop's own-brand product is often almost the same as the famous brand but cheaper.» Why is the own brand often cheaper? | Because it comes from a farm | Because it is made of gold | Because it is always older | *Because you pay extra for the famous name and its adverts
exam: Which sentence uses brand as a verb, a doing word? | The shop sells a brand of cereal | The logo is printed on the box | A brand-new bed is warm and soft | *The farmer will brand the young calves
